{
    "chapter_num": 6,
    "verses_count": 22,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Decree of Darius"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then King Darius issued a decree, and a search was made in the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. house of the scrolls"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "archives, where the treasures were stored in Babylon. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And at "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Probably Ecbatana, the ancient capital of Media"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Achmetha, in the palace that "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in the province of Media, a scroll was found, and in it a record "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " written thus:"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "In the first year of King Cyrus, King Cyrus issued a decree "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "concerning"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " the house of God at Jerusalem: “Let the house be rebuilt, the place where they offered sacrifices; and let the foundations of it be firmly laid, its height sixty cubits "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "and"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " its width sixty cubits, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "with"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " three rows of heavy stones and one row of new timber. Let the expenses be paid from the king’s treasury. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Also let the gold and silver articles of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar took from the temple which "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in Jerusalem and brought to Babylon, be restored and taken back to the temple which "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "is"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in Jerusalem, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "each"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " to its place; and deposit "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "them"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in the house of God”—"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "therefore,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Tattenai, governor of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "the region"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " beyond the River, and Shethar-Boznai, and your companions the Persians who "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "are"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " beyond the River, keep yourselves far from there. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Let the work of this house of God alone; let the governor of the Jews and the elders of the Jews build this house of God on its site."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Moreover I issue a decree "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "as to"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " what you shall do for the elders of these Jews, for the building of this "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Temple"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "house of God: Let the cost be paid at the king’s expense from taxes "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "on the region"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " beyond the River; this is to be given immediately to these men, so that they are not hindered. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And whatever they need—young bulls, rams, and lambs for the burnt offerings of the God of heaven, wheat, salt, wine, and oil, according to the request of the priests who "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "are"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in Jerusalem—let it be given them day by day without fail, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "that they may offer sacrifices of sweet aroma to the God of heaven, and pray for the life of the king and his sons."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Also I issue a decree that whoever alters this edict, let a timber be pulled from his house and erected, and let him be hanged on it; and let his house be made a refuse heap because of this. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And may the God who causes His name to dwell there destroy any king or people who put their hand to alter it, or to destroy this "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Temple"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "house of God which is in Jerusalem. I Darius issue a decree; let it be done diligently."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Temple Completed and Dedicated"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then Tattenai, governor of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "the region"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " beyond the River, Shethar-Boznai, and their companions diligently did according to what King Darius had sent. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So the elders of the Jews built, and they prospered through the prophesying of Haggai the prophet and Zechariah the son of Iddo. And they built and finished "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "it,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " according to the commandment of the God of Israel, and according to the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "decree"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "command of Cyrus, Darius, and Artaxerxes king of Persia. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now the temple was finished on the third day of the month of Adar, which was in the sixth year of the reign of King Darius. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then the children of Israel, the priests and the Levites and the rest of the descendants of the captivity, celebrated the dedication of this "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Temple"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "house of God with joy. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And they offered sacrifices at the dedication of this house of God, one hundred bulls, two hundred rams, four hundred lambs, and as a sin offering for all Israel twelve male goats, according to the number of the tribes of Israel. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "They assigned the priests to their divisions and the Levites to their divisions, over the service of God in Jerusalem, as it is written in the Book of Moses."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Passover Celebrated"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "The Hebrew language resumes in Ezra 6:19 and continues through 7:11."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the descendants of the captivity kept the Passover on the fourteenth "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "day"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " of the first month. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For the priests and the Levites had purified themselves; all of them "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were ritually"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " clean. And they slaughtered the Passover "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "lambs"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " for all the descendants of the captivity, for their brethren the priests, and for themselves. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then the children of Israel who had returned from the captivity ate together with all who had separated themselves from the filth"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "uncleanness"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " of the nations of the land in order to seek the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " God of Israel. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And they kept the Feast of Unleavened Bread seven days with joy; for the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "DIVINE_NAME",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " made them joyful, and turned the heart of the king of Assyria toward them, to strengthen their hands in the work of the house of God, the God of Israel."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}